WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.233
People talk to an AI assistant in three places:

00:00:04.233 --> 00:00:08.380
a chat page in the admin, a floating chat on every admin page,

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.637
and a chat box on your website.

00:00:10.637 --> 00:00:14.845
This video shows why they exist, how each one works, and how to

00:00:14.845 --> 00:00:18.810
set them up, including the engines that can power the chat.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.296
Once an assistant exists, people need a place to talk to it.

00:00:27.296 --> 00:00:32.125
Staff want an answer without leaving their work, and visitors want an answer

00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:33.950
without writing an email.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.750
A chat has to remember the conversation, so a follow-up question makes sense,

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:44.130
and it has to keep a history, so nobody asks the same thing twice.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.523
It also has to work where people already are:

00:00:47.523 --> 00:00:50.840
in the admin, in a corner of every page, and on the public

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.950
site, limited to the people who are allowed to use it.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.327
The AI Chat module gives you all of that on top of your

00:00:58.327 --> 00:01:02.310
AI profiles, so an assistant behaves the same way everywhere.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:10.646
The chat page is one page for every chat profile, with a history

00:01:10.646 --> 00:01:12.537
of your own conversations.

00:01:12.537 --> 00:01:14.960
People open it from the admin menu.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:19.823
The admin chat widget floats on every admin page, so staff can ask

00:01:19.823 --> 00:01:22.851
a question without leaving what they are doing.

00:01:22.851 --> 00:01:26.050
You choose its profile once, in the site settings.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.923
The website chat widget is a normal widget that you place on a layer.

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:35.100
It puts an assistant in the corner of your public pages, for visitors.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:39.371
The engine behind a chat is called an orchestrator.

00:01:39.371 --> 00:01:44.374
The default one plans each answer, and two optional ones, Claude and GitHub

00:01:44.374 --> 00:01:47.030
Copilot, can take over for a profile.

00:01:51.281 --> 00:01:54.040
Open Artificial Intelligence, Profiles.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:58.024
Open the Actions menu of a chat profile and click New chat.

00:01:58.024 --> 00:02:02.437
A profile that has Show on admin menu turned on also appears under

00:02:02.437 --> 00:02:05.011
Artificial Intelligence in the menu.

00:02:06.584 --> 00:02:10.347
A new chat opens with the profile's welcome message.

00:02:10.347 --> 00:02:14.694
New Chat starts over, and Chat History lists your past chats.

00:02:15.155 --> 00:02:18.907
Type a question and press Enter, or click the send arrow.

00:02:18.907 --> 00:02:23.492
The answer appears as it is written, and it comes from the instructions

00:02:23.492 --> 00:02:25.815
and the knowledge of the profile.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.943
Ask a follow-up question.

00:02:27.943 --> 00:02:32.022
The assistant remembers what was said earlier in the same chat, so you

00:02:32.022 --> 00:02:33.579
do not repeat yourself.

00:02:34.038 --> 00:02:37.580
A chat is saved as soon as it starts, with a title that

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.019
the AI writes from the conversation.

00:02:40.019 --> 00:02:42.458
Click Chat History to find it later.

00:02:46.698 --> 00:02:51.388
Chat History lists your chats with this assistant, newest first.

00:02:51.388 --> 00:02:56.078
Each row shows its title, its status, and when it was last used.

00:02:56.581 --> 00:03:01.662
Type part of a title in History search and click Search to find a chat.

00:03:01.662 --> 00:03:06.611
Click View, or the title, to open it and continue where you left off.

00:03:07.172 --> 00:03:09.818
Actions on a row deletes that one chat.

00:03:09.818 --> 00:03:14.051
Delete Chat History deletes all of your chats with this assistant.

00:03:14.051 --> 00:03:17.872
Both ask you to confirm, and each needs its own permission.

00:03:18.365 --> 00:03:21.147
New Chat starts over with an empty chat.

00:03:21.147 --> 00:03:23.505
You only ever see your own chats.

00:03:27.691 --> 00:03:33.618
Turn on the AI Chat Admin Widget feature, then open Settings, Artificial Intelligence.

00:03:33.618 --> 00:03:38.901
The Admin Widget section decides which assistant floats on every admin page.

00:03:39.356 --> 00:03:41.135
Pick the Chat profile.

00:03:41.135 --> 00:03:43.867
Choose No profile to hide the widget.

00:03:43.867 --> 00:03:48.696
Max history sessions and Primary color appear once you pick a profile.

00:03:48.696 --> 00:03:49.776
Click Save.

00:03:50.226 --> 00:03:54.771
Now every admin page has a round chat button in the bottom-right corner.

00:03:54.771 --> 00:03:56.926
Click it to open the assistant.

00:03:57.378 --> 00:04:00.067
Ask a question without leaving the page.

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:03.984
The widget has the same message box as the chat page, and its

00:04:03.984 --> 00:04:06.498
header has New chat and Chat history.

00:04:06.951 --> 00:04:11.651
Drag the header to move the window, and drag its edge to resize it.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:17.251
The widget remembers its place, its size, and your current chat on the next page.

00:04:21.445 --> 00:04:27.051
To put an assistant on your public website, use the Artificial Intelligence Chat widget.

00:04:27.051 --> 00:04:28.662
Open Design, Widgets.

00:04:28.662 --> 00:04:32.836
A zone is where a widget lives, here Footer, and a layer decides

00:04:32.836 --> 00:04:34.625
on which pages it shows.

00:04:35.079 --> 00:04:39.801
The Always layer has one rule, a Boolean condition set to true, so

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:42.228
its widgets show on every page.

00:04:42.228 --> 00:04:45.179
Click Edit on a layer to see its rules.

00:04:45.631 --> 00:04:49.800
Back on the Widgets page, open Add Widget in the Footer zone and

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.301
choose Artificial Intelligence Chat.

00:04:52.751 --> 00:04:57.780
Give the widget a Title, pick the layer, and pick the Profile it talks to.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:03.374
Total history chat to show sets how many past chats a signed-in visitor can reopen.

00:05:03.374 --> 00:05:04.631
Click Publish.

00:05:05.082 --> 00:05:06.423
Open your website.

00:05:06.423 --> 00:05:08.938
A round chat button sits in the corner.

00:05:08.938 --> 00:05:13.017
Visitors who are not signed in use the Anonymous role, so give that

00:05:13.017 --> 00:05:16.482
role permission to query this one profile, and no other.

00:05:16.938 --> 00:05:18.957
Visitors chat the same way.

00:05:18.957 --> 00:05:23.360
A chat is saved only once the visitor sends a first message, never

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.868
just because someone opened a page.

00:05:30.057 --> 00:05:35.454
The engine that plans an answer and decides which tools to use is called an orchestrator.

00:05:35.454 --> 00:05:41.817
Settings, Artificial Intelligence has a Default Orchestrator section for the one that comes with the site.

00:05:42.271 --> 00:05:46.351
The AI Claude Orchestrator feature adds a Claude section.

00:05:46.351 --> 00:05:51.985
Choose the Authentication type, API key, enter the key, and pick a Default model.

00:05:51.985 --> 00:05:55.611
Claude stays off while the type is Not configured.

00:05:56.064 --> 00:06:00.634
The AI Copilot Orchestrator feature adds a Copilot section.

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:05.203
It signs in as a GitHub signed-in user, or it uses your own

00:06:05.203 --> 00:06:09.984
API key, with a Provider type, a Base URL and a Default model.

00:06:10.437 --> 00:06:14.004
Once an engine is set up, a profile can choose it in the

00:06:14.004 --> 00:06:16.592
Orchestrator field of its General card.

00:06:16.592 --> 00:06:22.057
Those engines choose their own model, so the deployment fields of the profile are hidden.

00:06:26.246 --> 00:06:30.083
A public assistant is open to anyone, so the site protects it.

00:06:30.083 --> 00:06:34.598
In the Prompt Security section, checks block messages that try to make the

00:06:34.598 --> 00:06:36.856
assistant ignore its instructions.

00:06:37.308 --> 00:06:39.276
Below them are the limits:

00:06:39.276 --> 00:06:43.579
how many messages one person can send in a window, and tiers for

00:06:43.579 --> 00:06:48.374
visitors who are not signed in, such as a short burst and a daily total.

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:52.308
Session limits cap how many new chats a visitor can start.

00:06:52.763 --> 00:06:58.947
The Visitor Identity section decides how a visitor is recognized across visits, with a cookie.

00:06:58.947 --> 00:07:02.533
Set the Visitor cookie name and the Cookie lifetime.

00:07:02.987 --> 00:07:07.592
A profile can override these limits on its own Prompt Security card.

00:07:07.592 --> 00:07:10.767
Leave a field empty to keep the site's value.

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:17.134
Staff get an internal helper.

00:07:17.134 --> 00:07:21.532
A policy assistant is one click away in the admin menu, and every

00:07:21.532 --> 00:07:24.877
conversation is kept for the person who held it.

00:07:25.627 --> 00:07:27.889
Visitors get a website assistant.

00:07:27.889 --> 00:07:32.704
It answers questions about opening hours, orders and repairs at any time, and

00:07:32.704 --> 00:07:34.967
hands over when it does not know.

00:07:35.717 --> 00:07:38.911
Editors get an admin assistant that is always there.

00:07:38.911 --> 00:07:43.537
Give its profile tools, and it can look things up on the site while they work.

00:07:44.287 --> 00:07:48.812
A team that already uses Claude or GitHub Copilot can pick that engine

00:07:48.812 --> 00:07:52.207
for one profile, and keep the default for the rest.

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:58.260
A chat page for staff, a floating chat in the admin, and a

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:01.680
chat box for visitors, all on the same profiles.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.327
Thanks for watching.

